WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.400
Alright, so in this video we're going to do a detailed tutorial on Agent Mode.

00:04.500 --> 00:07.300
You can trigger Agent Mode either by clicking the notch at the top

00:07.400 --> 00:10.200
or pressing the command button and speaking.

00:10.900 --> 00:12.500
Hey, can you hear me?

00:16.000 --> 00:19.800
Yes, I can hear you loud and clear. How can I help you tonight, Jonah?

00:20.200 --> 00:23.900
And then you can configure it by clicking Agent right here in the sidebar.

00:24.000 --> 00:25.300
There's several things we can do.

00:25.400 --> 00:27.300
We can change the agent voice,

00:27.400 --> 00:30.300
information that he knows about you, such as your first and last name,

00:30.400 --> 00:34.200
and then his memories will start to accumulate as you start using Agent Mode.

00:34.900 --> 00:35.900
Then we have actions.

00:36.000 --> 00:38.900
These are system actions that can be performed on a computer,

00:39.200 --> 00:41.500
such as opening an app, setting the volume.

00:41.800 --> 00:45.400
Viewing the screen and writing into apps are by default set to false,

00:45.500 --> 00:49.500
but if you trigger them, you can essentially ask any question about your screen.

00:50.000 --> 00:51.800
Hey, what does this mean?

00:52.300 --> 00:57.400
You can see I use my cursor to select this part, and it will actually isolate this.

00:57.500 --> 00:58.700
What are we looking at?

00:58.900 --> 01:02.800
That action allows me to play, pause, or skip tracks on your active media player

01:02.900 --> 01:05.000
whenever you ask me to control your music.

01:05.800 --> 01:06.800
Sweet.

01:07.200 --> 01:08.800
And then lastly, we have integrations.

01:08.900 --> 01:10.500
This lets you connect your apps with VoiceOS,

01:10.600 --> 01:14.400
so you can send a message, schedule a meeting,

01:14.500 --> 01:16.900
or send an email simply by using your voice.

01:17.000 --> 01:20.900
If you're a power user and want to use your own MCP, we're looking for you.

01:21.300 --> 01:24.200
We actually built this right here in the advanced section.

01:25.000 --> 01:28.500
By expanding this, you can see that you can connect your own custom MCPs

01:28.600 --> 01:30.700
to do much more than the integrations that we offer.

01:30.800 --> 01:32.900
Literally anything you can think of.

01:34.000 --> 01:35.600
Alright, I think this concludes the tutorial.

01:35.800 --> 01:38.500
If you have any other questions, feel free to shoot me an email right here,

01:38.600 --> 01:40.500
or book a meeting with me. Thanks!
